---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="StretchesFor processes questionnaire answers only in temporary browser memory and collects no medical history.">
  <article class="container-shell py-14 sm:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-success">No account. No health profile.</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-balance text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.05em] sm:text-6xl">Privacy by absence.</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-pretty text-lg leading-8 text-muted">The simplest way to protect sensitive answers is not to collect them.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-sf mt-14 max-w-3xl">
      <h2>Questionnaire answers</h2>
      <p>Your body-area choice and questionnaire answers exist only in the current page’s memory. They are not sent to an API, written to a database, placed in the URL, or saved in browser storage. Refreshing or closing the page clears them.</p>
      <h2>Voice guidance</h2>
      <p>Optional voice guidance uses the browser’s built-in speech synthesis feature. StretchesFor does not record your voice, request microphone access, or send questionnaire text to its own backend.</p>
      <h2>Accounts and records</h2>
      <p>There are no accounts, profiles, saved routines, medical records, feedback forms, or email collection.</p>
      <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>This version does not use third-party analytics, advertising pixels, behavioural tracking, or marketing cookies.</p>
      <h2>Hosting logs</h2>
      <p>Like most websites, the hosting provider may process basic technical request logs for security and reliable delivery. StretchesFor does not combine those logs with questionnaire answers because questionnaire answers never leave the browser.</p>
      <h2>Contact and changes</h2>
      <p>A future contact method or material privacy change must be reflected on this page before collection begins. Last updated 29 August 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
